IMPORT prelude

-- Graffiti Vandalism Act 2016 (WA) -- date helpers for the core and the seat layer.
--
-- This module states no rule of the Graffiti Vandalism Act. It holds the date helpers the other modules need, built
-- on the built-in DATE functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_YEAR), and the two counting rules
-- of the Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) that the Act's periods need: s 61(1)(b) (the first day left out) and s 61(1)(e)
-- (a last day on an excluded day moves to the next day that is not one), with the excluded days of s 61(2). It does
-- not IMPORT daydate, so no other module needs daydate either, and daydate's operator overloads on DATE never meet the
-- Act's arithmetic.
--
-- Time on the regulative rules' timeline is counted in whole days, as day numbers (DATE_SERIAL). A rule's trace
-- starts on the day number of the day its period runs from, and its WITHIN is a number of days. On the stable l4 an
-- event on the start day plus WITHIN is still within the period, which is how the Interpretation Act 1984 (WA)
-- s 61(1)(b) counts a period "after" a day: the day itself is left out, and the last day is that day plus the
-- number of days. Where s 61(1)(e) moves the last day, the WITHIN is the days from the start to the moved last day.
-- (The entry rule in ss 27-28 counts in minutes instead; see gva-core.l4.)
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Date helpers`

-- YMD is not in the stable prelude (ENCODING-GUIDE section 5); this is the local shim, on the built-in.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y` -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

-- The day number of a date: the time on the regulative rules' timeline.
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` `the date` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the date`

-- The date that is a number of days after another date (Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b): the first day is left
-- out, so 28 days after 1 March is 29 March).
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER, `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the days` `days after` `the date` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the date` PLUS `the days`)

-- How many days a later date is after an earlier one (negative if it is before it).
GIVEN `the earlier date` IS A DATE, `the later date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the earlier date` `to` `the later date` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the later date` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the earlier date`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is after` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is the same day as` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `other`

§ `Excluded days (Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(e), (2); Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 s 5, Second Schedule)`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(e): "where the time limited for the doing of a thing expires or falls upon an
-- excluded day, the thing may be done on the next day that is not an excluded day". s 61(2): "excluded day means
-- Saturday, Sunday, public service holiday, and a bank holiday or public holiday throughout the State or in that part of
-- the State which is relevant to the event, act, thing or proceeding concerned."
--
-- The public holidays throughout the State are the days of the Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 s 5 and Second
-- Schedule (deposited at subjects/au/wa/public-and-bank-holidays-act-1972/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_44571.txt).
-- Counted here: every Saturday and Sunday, and every Schedule day that is fixed or worked out from the calendar.
-- NOT counted, because nothing deposited fixes them: the Celebration Day for the Birthday of the Reigning Sovereign
-- (the King's Birthday, "appointed for each year by proclamation"), special or substituted days proclaimed under the
-- Public and Bank Holidays Act ss 7 and 8, public service holidays, and holidays in only part of the State (NOTES.md
-- finding 11). The Saturday bank holiday of that Act's s 6 is a Saturday already.
--
-- The Schedule's days are worked out as in the baseline encoding of that Act
-- (subjects/au/wa/public-and-bank-holidays-act-1972/encodings/baseline-2026-10/pbha-holidays.l4), restated here because
-- an l4 module cannot be imported from another folder. Easter is that encoding's choice too: the Act names Good Friday,
-- Easter Sunday and Easter Monday without saying how Easter is fixed, and the Gregorian computus gives the Western
-- churches' Easter.

-- The day of the week: DATE_SERIAL modulo 7 is 0 on a Sunday and 6 on a Saturday (1 January 2027, a Friday, is 5).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is a Saturday or Sunday` IF
    `the weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 6 OR `the weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 0

-- The Schedule's "Monday on or first Monday following" a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Monday on or first Monday following` `the day` MEANS
    ((8 MINUS `the weekday of` `the day`) MODULO 7) `days after` `the day`

-- The Schedule's "the next following Tuesday": strictly after the day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next following Tuesday after` `the day` MEANS
    (((8 MINUS `the weekday of` `the day`) MODULO 7) PLUS 1) `days after` `the day`

-- Easter Sunday by the Gregorian computus (the anonymous Gregorian algorithm).
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` `the year` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY ((r MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR (r DIVIDED BY 31)) `the year`
    WHERE
        a MEANS `the year` MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (`the year` DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS `the year` MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)
        r MEANS h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114

-- Second Schedule: "New Year's Day (1st January). Australia Day (26th January or, when that day falls on a Saturday or
-- Sunday, the first Monday following the 26th January). Labour Day (Monday on or first Monday following the 1st
-- March). Good Friday. Easter Sunday. Easter Monday. Anzac Day (25th April). Western Australia Day (Monday on or first
-- Monday following the 1st June). [The Sovereign's birthday, by proclamation: not counted.] Christmas Day (25th
-- December). Boxing Day (26th December). When New Year's Day, Anzac Day, or Christmas Day falls on a Saturday or Sunday
-- the next following Monday is also a public holiday and bank holiday. When Boxing Day falls on a Saturday the next
-- following Monday is also a public holiday and bank holiday. When Boxing Day falls on a Sunday or Monday the next
-- following Tuesday is also a public holiday and bank holiday."
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is a public holiday in the Second Schedule, other than one appointed by proclamation` IF
        `the day` `is the same day as` `New Year's Day`
    OR (`New Year's Day` `is a Saturday or Sunday` AND `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` `New Year's Day`))
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` `Australia Day`
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 `the year of the day`))
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` (2 `days before` `Easter Sunday`)
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` `Easter Sunday`
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` (1 `days after` `Easter Sunday`)
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` `Anzac Day`
    OR (`Anzac Day` `is a Saturday or Sunday` AND `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` `Anzac Day`))
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 `the year of the day`))
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` `Christmas Day`
    OR `the day` `is the same day as` `Boxing Day`
    OR (`Christmas Day` `is a Saturday or Sunday` AND `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` `Christmas Day`))
    OR (`the weekday of` `Boxing Day` EQUALS 6 AND `the day` `is the same day as` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` `Boxing Day`))
    OR (    (`the weekday of` `Boxing Day` EQUALS 0 OR `the weekday of` `Boxing Day` EQUALS 1)
        AND `the day` `is the same day as` (`the next following Tuesday after` `Boxing Day`))
    WHERE
        `the year of the day` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day`
        `New Year's Day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 `the year of the day`
        `Australia Day` MEANS
            IF (DATE_FROM_DMY 26 1 `the year of the day`) `is a Saturday or Sunday`
            THEN `the Monday on or first Monday following` (DATE_FROM_DMY 26 1 `the year of the day`)
            ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 26 1 `the year of the day`
        `Easter Sunday` MEANS `Easter Sunday in` `the year of the day`
        `Anzac Day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 4 `the year of the day`
        `Christmas Day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 12 `the year of the day`
        `Boxing Day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 26 12 `the year of the day`

-- The date that is a number of days before another date.
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER, `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the days` `days before` `the date` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the date` MINUS `the days`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is an excluded day` IF
    `the day` `is a Saturday or Sunday` OR `the day` `is a public holiday in the Second Schedule, other than one appointed by proclamation`

-- s 61(1)(e): the last day of a period, or, if it is an excluded day, the next day that is not one.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Interpretation Act s 61(1)(e) -- the last day, or the next day that is not an excluded day` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` `is an excluded day`
    THEN `Interpretation Act s 61(1)(e) -- the last day, or the next day that is not an excluded day` (1 `days after` `the day`)
    ELSE `the day`
